{
  "id": 5,
  "title": "Food & drink",
  "goal": "Order food and drinks, say what you want and don't want, and say what you like.",
  "intro": "Kerala food is built around **rice** (ചോറ് *chōṟŭ*), coconut, fish and spices; breakfast staples include **puttu**, **appam** and **dosa**. 'Have you eaten?' (ഭക്ഷണം കഴിച്ചോ? / ചോറുണ്ടോ?) is a standard friendly greeting.\n\nGrammatically, this unit introduces a key Malayalam pattern: the **dative subject**. 'I want', 'I like', 'I'm hungry' are expressed as 'to me there is want / liking / hunger': എനിക്ക് വേണം, എനിക്ക് ഇഷ്ടമാണ്, എനിക്ക് വിശക്കുന്നു.",
